course: dictionary
lesson: 12261
title: Words that mean "at the same time"
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Contemporaneous is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Contemporary means belonging to the same time, so contemporaneous means existing or happening at the same time as something else. «The two poets were contemporaneous, both writing in the same century.»
explain: It can also describe a record that was written at the time something happened, not later. «Her contemporaneous diary described the storm as it hit the village.» She wrote it that night, so it tells you small details more reliably than a story told many years later.
explain: Historians call these records contemporaneous sources, or primary sources. Diaries, letters and newspapers from the time are examples. When you meet this word, look for the clue: it always links things that happen together, or records made at the same moment.
fact: Contemporaneous means existing or happening at the same time as something else.
fact: Contemporaneous notes are written down at the time something happened, not later.
fact: Contemporaneous is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in writing, not in everyday chat.
fact: Historians often trust contemporaneous sources, such as diaries and letters, more about small details.
fact: Contemporaneous sources are also called primary sources, or contemporary sources.
exercise: «The two accounts of the flood were contemporaneous, both written in the same week.» What does contemporaneous mean here? | Very large | Lost forever | *Happening at the same time | Written by a famous author
exercise: A historian wants the most trustworthy detail about a battle. Which source is contemporaneous? | *A letter written by a soldier on the day of the battle | A film made 200 years later | A story a grandparent told in old age | A book of made-up adventures
exercise: Which word means written at the time something happened, not later? | Imagined | *Contemporaneous | Later | Remembered
test: «Police wrote contemporaneous notes as the crash happened.» What does this tell you? | The notes were written years later | The notes were drawn with pictures | The notes were lost | *The notes were written at the time, as it happened
test: Which of these is another name for contemporaneous sources? | Broken sources | Future sources | Secret sources | *Primary sources
exam: Which sentence uses contemporaneous correctly? | The contemporaneous sandwich was eaten quickly | He felt contemporaneous and very tall | She was contemporaneous with her favourite pizza | *Her letters and the newspaper report of the fire were contemporaneous
